# freeware/ is the public-domain disk image shipped with os9exec.
# h5 is a symlink -> freeware (repo-root convention post h0/h1 reorg).
# freeware/ content is gitignored until proprietary items are fully removed.
freeware
# h? not h*: the disk mounts are all two characters (h0 h1 h4 he, test/h8..hd).
# h* also matched any FILE starting with h -- and on a case-insensitive
# filesystem, with H too, so e.g. a HANDOFF.md silently refused to be added.
h?
dd

# os9defs/ headers are OURS: reconstructed from books and documentation found
# online, using the information rather than any Microware source. Copyrighted
# facts, not stolen code -- so they are committed. (They are also second-hand
# and not guaranteed Microware-compatible; each header says so at the top.)
# The proprietary Microware headers that once lived here are gone, so there is
# nothing left in that directory to exclude.

# Adapted OS-9 headers (user-derived from originals; not redistributable pending permission)
/Source/OS9exec_core/os9defs/orig/

# Build output
/Output/
/build/
/.build/
/os9exec
/os9exec.exe
/dist/
/test/.build/

# Reference PDFs and research material (large, not redistributable)
/resources/

# Claude Code per-user local settings (machine-specific allowlist)
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Internal planning docs — not ready for public visibility yet
# (index + the per-architecture splits ROADMAP-68k.md / ROADMAP-6809.md)
/ROADMAP*.md

# Session-to-session handoff/continuity notes — for the pair, not the community
*HANDOFF.md
*NEXT-SESSION.md

# Subagent-driven-development scratch state (progress ledger, review packages)
/.superpowers/
